      text: 'Some people propose that tenants\' deposits should be held by an independent body rather than by the landlord. Supporters say that a landlord who keeps the money loses nothing by ( 1 ) and point to a scheme in England and Wales that offers a free service for settling disputes, while opponents argue that a scheme would add costs and paperwork and could slow down urgent repairs. The writer supports such a rule, combined with a dated record of the flat\'s ( 2 ) signed by both sides and written explanations of any ( 3 ).',
