    qa: [
      { q: 'Why were the raised edges of the tablets useful?', choices: ['They made the tablets much lighter.', 'They held the stylus when not in use.', 'They kept the wax from rubbing.', 'They showed the name of the tablet\'s owner.'], answer: 2, why: '第4段落：高くしたふちのおかげで、板をとじたときにろうの面どうしがこすれなかったとある。' },
      { q: 'According to the passage, why can scholars still read some old tablets?', choices: ['The wax was kept in cold cellars.', 'Scratches reached the wood below.', 'The writing was copied onto paper.', 'Their owners wrote in very dark ink.'], answer: 1, why: '第5・6段落：スタイラスを強くおしつけると下の木に傷が残り、その傷から文が読めたとある。' },
    ],
