    qa: [
      { q: 'Why were railway companies slow to change their couplers?', choices: ['Workers refused to learn the new system.', 'The knuckle coupler was not strong enough.', 'The government had banned all new designs.', 'New equipment was expensive.'], answer: 3, why: '第3段落：新しい装置が高価だったためとある。作業員が拒んだ、強さが足りない、政府が禁じたとは書かれていない。' },
      { q: 'What does the passage say about Japan in 1925?', choices: ['It went back to the link and pin system.', 'Couplers were replaced very fast.', 'It bought all of its new cars from Europe.', 'It stopped using freight trains on Honshu.'], answer: 1, why: '第5段落：おどろくほど短い期間で自動連結器に取りかえ、本州ではほとんど一日で終わったとある。' },
    ],
