    qa: [
      { q: 'Why, according to the writer, did strangers help more readily?', choices: ['The writer asked every stranger for help out loud', 'The writer had become well known in the area', 'The stick made a need visible', 'The trains were much less crowded than usual'], answer: 2, why: '第4段落 The stick seemed to make a need visible, and visible needs are easier to answer。' },
      { q: 'What point does the writer make with poles on mountain trails?', choices: ['The same object can suggest confidence', 'Mountain poles are heavier than walking sticks', 'Hikers should never carry more than one pole', 'Poles were first a sign of fashion'], answer: 0, why: '第6段落 The same object, it seems, can suggest weakness in one setting and confidence in another。' },
    ],
