      text: 'In 2025, the UK regulator allowed banks to set their own limits for contactless card payments instead of following one fixed ( 1 ). Supporters say higher prices make the old limit inconvenient and that banks can judge risk for each customer. Opponents fear larger losses when cards are stolen and ( 2 ) among customers who hold cards from different banks. The writer accepts the change but wants sensible ( 3 ) limits for new cards and clear ways to lower them.',
