      text: 'Since 2021, American hospitals have had to publish their prices, including the rates agreed with insurers. Supporters say this lets patients ( 1 ) hospitals and allows researchers to study why prices differ. Opponents note that patients often cannot choose, that the files are hard to use and costly to prepare, and that price says nothing about ( 2 ). The writer wants the rules strengthened by requiring a common format and by making it easy for each patient to learn what they will actually ( 3 ).',
