    qa: [
      { q: 'Why is Cyttaria found only in certain parts of the world?', choices: ['It needs the sugar found only in Patagonian insects', 'Darwin carried it only to a few southern islands', 'It can live only on southern beech trees', 'Its spores cannot survive in cold forests'], answer: 2, why: '第2段落：ナンキョクブナにしか生きられないため、この木が生える場所でしか見られないとある。' },
      { q: 'What did the discovery about the wild yeast suggest?', choices: ['Beer was first brewed in South American beech forests', 'Cyttaria itself can be used in place of yeast to make beer', 'European yeasts had spread to Patagonia long ago', 'A parent of lager yeast may have come from Patagonia'], answer: 3, why: '第6段落：ラガービール酵母の親の一つが、遠い南の森から来たのかもしれないことを示したとある。' },
    ],
