    qa: [
      { q: 'Why were many outside fire escapes added to existing buildings?', choices: ['It was the cheapest way to add a route', 'Residents wanted more space to grow plants', 'Inside stairs were banned in tall buildings', 'Iron had become cheaper than wood or brick'], answer: 0, why: '第2段落 the cheapest way to provide one in an existing building was to hang it on the outside wall。' },
      { q: 'What does the writer say about a fire escape\'s main job?', choices: ['It matters far less than its use as a garden', 'It is to give people a place to dry washing', 'It succeeds most when it is never needed', 'It was done badly during the long power cut'], answer: 2, why: '第6段落 a fire escape is most successful when its main job is never needed at all。' },
    ],
