    qa: [
      { q: 'Why is the kawahagi called a bait thief?', choices: ['It steals fish that anglers keep in their buckets', 'It eats only fishing bait', 'It picks off bait without taking the hook', 'It follows boats to eat the waste that is thrown out'], answer: 2, why: '第3段落：針そのものは口に入れずに、えさを少しずつつつきとってしまうとある。' },
      { q: 'What is one difficulty in farming kawahagi?', choices: ['Young fish may bite each other in tanks', 'The liver becomes too small', 'Farmed fish lose their spines and cannot survive at all', 'Markets refuse to buy fish that were raised in farms'], answer: 0, why: '第6段落：こみあった水そうで育てると、若い魚どうしがするどい歯でかみ合ってしまうことがあるとある。' },
    ],
