    qa: [
      { q: 'Why did builders use cement mortar to repair older walls?', choices: ['It was the only mortar that could be bought', 'Lime had been banned for use in old buildings', 'It let moisture pass through more easily', 'They thought it would make them stronger'], answer: 3, why: '第4段落 assuming that a stronger mortar would make a stronger wall。' },
      { q: 'What can happen to fine cracks in lime mortar?', choices: ['They can close up over time', 'They let the bricks absorb gravel', 'They make the wall much heavier', 'They turn the mortar into cement'], answer: 0, why: '第6段落 Fine cracks in lime mortar can even close over time, as water dissolves a little lime and deposits it again inside the gaps。' },
    ],
