    qa: [
      { q: 'Why did the neighbor recommend swinging the mop in a figure eight?', choices: ['It uses much less water than straight lines', 'It stops the wooden handle from bending further', 'It lets the floor dry before anyone walks on it', 'The curve gathers dirt instead of pushing it'], answer: 3, why: '第4段落 because the curve gathers dirt instead of simply driving it forward。' },
      { q: 'How does the writer come to regard the old mop at the end?', choices: ['As a tool that should be replaced very soon', 'As a quiet invitation to deal with shared space', 'As a reminder of the neighbor\'s former office job', 'As something that belongs to the cleaning staff alone'], answer: 1, why: '第7段落 I think of it less as a cleaning tool than as a quiet invitation。' },
    ],
