    qa: [
      { q: 'How is the fire moved up the kiln?', choices: ['Wood is fed into each chamber in turn', 'A fan pushes the flames upward', 'Workers carry burning coal from room to room', 'The chimney is opened wider every hour'], answer: 0, why: '第2段落 workers begin to feed wood through small openings in the side of the second chamber ... one chamber at a time。' },
      { q: 'Why are few climbing kilns still in regular use?', choices: ['The government banned them after the war', 'Wood is costly and smoke causes objections', 'Their chambers cannot hold many pieces', 'Potters no longer know how to build such kilns'], answer: 1, why: '第6段落 Wood has become expensive, and neighbors may object to the smoke from a large firing。' },
    ],
